            <div xml:id="d422">

                <pb facs="0565" n="463" sameAs="frus:frus1908/pg463"/>

                <note rend="inline" type="source">File No. 7357/294.</note>
                <head><hi rendition="#italic">The Acting Secretary of
                            State to Minister Dodge.</hi></head>
                <opener><dateline rendition="#float-right"><placeName><hi rendition="#small-caps"
                                >Department of State</hi>,<lb/><hi rendition="#italic"
                                >Washington</hi></placeName>, <date calendar="gregorian"
                            when="1908-08-14"><hi rendition="#italic">August 14,
                        1908</hi></date>.</dateline></opener>
                <p><hi rendition="#small-caps">Sir</hi>: I have to acknowledge the receipt of your
                    No. 32, Honduranean series, of the 28th ultimo, in regard to the cancellation of
                    the exequaturs of the American consul and vice consul at Ceiba, Honduras. You
                    state that, as it seemed advisable to have some one temporarily in charge of the
                    consulate there, you decided that upon the receipt of instructions from the
                    department you would ask the vice consul at Puerto Cortez to do so.</p>
                <p>In this connection reference is made to the department’s telegram of the 6th
                    instant stating that it did not seem advisable to place anyone in charge of the
                    consulate at Ceiba at present.</p>
                <p>I am, etc.,</p>
                <closer><signed><hi rendition="#small-caps">Alvey A. Adee.</hi></signed></closer>
            </div>
        </body>
    </text>
